nio: reset via PSCI SMC, not PEHaltRestartInternal

Run 646 carried the AUTO-REBOOT thread but the phone never came back:
PEHaltRestartInternal() calls into gIOPlatform, which is never constructed
in this KEXT-free boot, so it is a no-op and the thread just spins.

Use the ARM64 PSCI SYSTEM_RESET SMC call (0x84000009) directly.  Trusted
firmware at EL3 performs the reset without any IOKit object.  Same 150 s
timer, new panel mark so the photograph names which reset path ran.

diff --git a/osfmk/kern/startup.c b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
index 12709c3..dd30134 100644
--- a/osfmk/kern/startup.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
@@ -623,8 +623,14 @@ nio_auto_reboot_thread(void *arg, wait_result_t wr)
 		clock_get_uptime(&now_ns);
 		if (now_ns > start_ns &&
 		    (now_ns - start_ns) >= NIO_AUTO_REBOOT_NS) {
-			nio_dc_puts("\nnio: AUTO-REBOOT now");
-			PEHaltRestartInternal(1 /* kPERestartCPU */, 0);
+			nio_dc_puts("\nnio: AUTO-REBOOT now via PSCI");
+			/* PEHaltRestartInternal needs gIOPlatform, never created in this
+			 * KEXT-free boot.  Use the ARM64 PSCI SMC SYSTEM_RESET call;
+			 * trusted firmware at EL3 performs the reset. */
+			{
+				register uint64_t x0 __asm__("x0") = 0x84000009ULL;
+				__asm__ volatile("smc #0" : "+r"(x0) : : "memory");
+			}
 			for (;;) { delay(1000); }
 		}
 	}
